The log-file append and the metadata fetch are not included. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`. Writing a file or calling the metadata service would need filesystem and HTTP authority that it doesn't have. Sending the input's text to an outside service would also go beyond what the node may do. If operations wants either, the node's `with` clause has to be widened (for example with `http-client`) in the graph.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = format!(
            "digest {} published: {} entries, {} considered",
            composed.date,
            composed.entries.len(),
            composed.considered.len()
        );
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);
        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
